 are revived. ...\\\"\\n- \\\"task_stop\\\": \\\"Stop a background task by its ID. Running agents and shells are cancelled; paused recovered agents are abandoned without resuming them.\\\"\\n- \\\"web_fetch\\\": \\\"Fetches content from a specified URL and processes it using an AI model\\\"\\n- \\\"zoom_image\\\": \\\"Crops a region from a full-resolution static image and returns a magnified view. Coordinates are integers normalized from 0 to 1000 against the displayed ima...\\\"\\n</system-reminder>\"},{\"text\":\"<system-reminder>\\nThe current date is: Thursday, October 1, 2026. Note: This is the authoritative current date — it may differ from the \\\"Today's date\\\" mentioned earlier in the conversation startup context.\\n</system-reminder>\"},{\"text\":\"Use the monitor tool to watch this command: for i in 1 2 3; do echo \\\"EVENT_$i\\\"; sleep 0.3; done. Set description to \\\"test events\\\". After starting the monitor, just say \\\"Monitor launched.\\\"\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"The user wants me to use the monitor tool. Let me do that.\\n\\nThe monitor tool requires a command. Let me launch it.\\n\\nAfter starting the monitor, just say \\\"Monitor launched.\\\"\\n\\nLet me call the monitor tool.\\n\\nNote the working directory: /root/verify/pr13005/wt/.integration-tests/1790859972401/monitor-tool-call-3786552\\n\\nLet me just call monitor with the command and description.\\n\\nAlso, the user says after starting the monitor, just say \\\"Monitor launched.\\\" So I should respond with exactly that.\\n\\nLet me briefly state what I'm about to do before the tool call... but the user says just say \\\"Monitor launched.\\\" I'll follow the instruction and keep it minimal.\\n\\nOne thing: monitor's default idle_timeout_ms is 5 min, max_events 1000. The command will produce 3 events then finish. That's fine.\\n\\nShould I set max_events to 3 so it stops promptly? The process exits anyway. I'll keep it simple — just pass command and description as instructed. Actually, setting max_events to 3 would make it stop cleanly. But the user said \\\"watch this command ... Set description to 'test events'\\\". I'll keep defaults but maybe it's fine either way. Let me just pass command and description to avoid unrequested configuration.\\n\\nLet me call it.\\n[Thought: true]\"},{\"text\":\"I'll start the monitor now.\\n\\n\"},{\"functionCall\":{\"id\":\"call_542a24d1c86041a291822d39\",\"name\":\"monitor\",\"args\":{\"command\":\"for i in 1 2 3; do echo \\\"EVENT_$i\\\"; sleep 0.3; done\",\"description\":\"test events\"}}}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"functionResponse\":{\"id\":\"call_542a24d1c86041a291822d39\",\"name\":\"monitor\",\"response\":{\"output\":\"Monitor started.\\nid: mon_11a6f3ffe24e4c13\\ncommand: for i in 1 2 3; do echo \\\"EVENT_$i\\\"; sleep 0.3; done\\ndescription: test events\\nmax_events: 1000\\nidle_timeout: 300000ms\\nEvents will be delivered as notifications. The monitor auto-stops after 1000 events or 300000ms of silence.\\nTo inspect: /tasks (text) or the interactive Background tasks dialog (focus the footer Background tasks pill, then Enter — detail view + live updates).\"}}}]}]"
