n as instructed. Actually, setting max_events to 3 would make it stop cleanly. But the user said \\\"watch this command ... Set description to 'test events'\\\". I'll keep defaults but maybe it's fine either way. Let me just pass command and description to avoid unrequested configuration.\\n\\nLet me call it.\\n[Thought: true]\"},{\"text\":\"I'll start the monitor now.\\n\\n\"},{\"functionCall\":{\"id\":\"call_542a24d1c86041a291822d39\",\"name\":\"monitor\",\"args\":{\"command\":\"for i in 1 2 3; do echo \\\"EVENT_$i\\\"; sleep 0.3; done\",\"description\":\"test events\"}}}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"functionResponse\":{\"id\":\"call_542a24d1c86041a291822d39\",\"name\":\"monitor\",\"response\":{\"output\":\"Monitor started.\\nid: mon_11a6f3ffe24e4c13\\ncommand: for i in 1 2 3; do echo \\\"EVENT_$i\\\"; sleep 0.3; done\\ndescription: test events\\nmax_events: 1000\\nidle_timeout: 300000ms\\nEvents will be delivered as notifications. The monitor auto-stops after 1000 events or 300000ms of silence.\\nTo inspect: /tasks (text) or the interactive Background tasks dialog (focus the footer Background tasks pill, then Enter — detail view + live updates).\"}}}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"The user said after starting the monitor, just say \\\"Monitor launched.\\\" So I should respond with exactly that. No further text.\\n[Thought: true]\"},{\"text\":\"Monitor launched.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"<task-notification>\\n<task-id>mon_11a6f3ffe24e4c13</task-id>\\n<tool-use-id>call_542a24d1c86041a291822d39</tool-use-id>\\n<kind>monitor</kind>\\n<status>running</status>\\n<event-count>1</event-count>\\n<summary>Monitor \\\"test events\\\" emitted event #1.</summary>\\n<result>EVENT_1</result>\\n</task-notification>\\n\\n<task-notification>\\n<task-id>mon_11a6f3ffe24e4c13</task-id>\\n<tool-use-id>call_542a24d1c86041a291822d39</tool-use-id>\\n<kind>monitor</kind>\\n<status>running</status>\\n<event-count>2</event-count>\\n<summary>Monitor \